==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Valiant Poseidon''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Almighty Poseidon''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
Poseidon has high speed, decent health and decent damage and his ability is very good. He is an excellent counter to strong Metal/Zombie foes ([[Super Metal Hippoe]], [[Sir Metal Seal]], [[Zir Zeal]], [[Zang Roo]], etc.) and this makes him a valuable unit on many Metal stages or Zombie stages, as metals and zombies tend to be melee pushers. His zombie killer also comes in handy for finishing off weaker Zombies.

However, take into account that one Poseidon isn't enough to completely halt foes from reaching your Cats, due to his slow attack speed. He also lacks the ability to do critical hits. This often means you will have to bring other dedicated units to finish off Metals. Despite this, his freeze still has a very high uptime of 53%, making him one of the best Zombie and Metal CC in the game, and you can permafreeze Metal or Zombie enemies with just 2, though it's precise so 3 would work better. This makes him incredible in stages such as [[Attack on Titanium (Insane)|Attack on Titanium]], where you can summon up to three Poseidons, and less useful, but still a huge help in stages such as [[Unholy Tempest (Insane)|Unholy Tempest]], where the main threat spawns immediately.

==='''Talents'''===
Poseidon's savage blow is to be seen as a much greater, yet less consistent attack buff. His average DPS grows considerably by an average of 1.6x, so this should be the most prioritized talent alongside attack up. While his average DPS does reach an impressive 19k at level 50, the main appeal of these talents is the whopping 267k potential DPH that they allow Poseidon to deal in a single savage blow. This figure is enough to severely cripple or even one shot most enemies, and at the right moments can completely turn the tide of battle. Essentially, this turns him into a mini-rusher version of Lasvoss, trading damage for consistency.

Dodge gives him a chance to survive bad match-ups such as Cadaver Bear and Zamelle, however, the low proc and short duration makes it not worth investing, if you do it anyways, it's better leaving it at level 1, as the only thing that changes between levels is the duration, not the proc chance. Even then, it is important to know that there are suitable alternatives without such a hefty investment.

Freeze resistance may come in handy, but has generally little use, as Poseidon can easily infiltrate Henry's blindspot, there are currently no metal enemies with the Freeze ability, and while it may be for countering Zir Zeal, Poseidon has a high number of knockbacks, letting him escape from it anyways, not to mention he also has a range advantage that you can utilize.

Health up can make it possible to use more or even all of his knockbacks and farm for another massive savage blow nuke. It's a fairly significant upgrade, especially for those who use him often.

